      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you only want a solid object waving around in the wind you can try 'Shader Vegetation 3.0' (5€ in the asset store).\nYou may also need Polybrush (free) for vertex painting.\nOne vertex color remains stable on the ground(or wall) and the other one is in motion. It is meant for trees and leaves but should work fine on any other object. More like a hack and not as versatile as DB but we all know how long it takes VRC to implement new stuff. It performs better than cloth and dynamic bones and may give similar results in a lot of situations like ropes or flags. If you have static/baked vegetation in your worlds and want them to move similar to speed trees on terrain it is perfect. Not sure if it respects wind zones but it has some nice parameters in it to simulate wind.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
